<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 6 March, from 1204 to 1957.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1204">1204 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">822 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Philip II of France takes Château Gaillard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French troops captured Richard the Lionheart's great castle above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> after a six-month siege, some climbing in through a latrine chute. Normandy fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> within months.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1820">1820 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Monroe signs the Missouri Compromise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Missouri was to enter the Union as a slave state and Maine as a free one, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> barred from the rest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana-purchase">Louisiana Purchase</a> north of 36°30'. The balance held for three decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1836">1836 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Alamo falls to Santa Anna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mexican troops stormed the mission at dawn after a 13-day siege, killing nearly all of its roughly 200 defenders, including Jim Bowie and Davy Crockett. 'Remember the Alamo' became the Texan battle cry.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1857">1857 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">169 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Supreme Court decides Dred Scott v. Sandford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chief Justice Roger Taney ruled that Black Americans could not be citizens and that Congress could not ban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the territories. The decision deepened the crisis that led to civil war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1930">1930 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">96 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Clarence Birdseye's frozen foods go on sale</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shops in Springfield, Massachusetts, began selling quick-frozen vegetables, fruit, fish and meat using Birdseye's process. Frozen food went on to transform shopping and diets.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ghana becomes independent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> became independent as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwame-nkrumah">Kwame Nkrumah</a>, the first sub-Saharan colony to win independence from a European power after the war. It inspired independence movements across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwame-nkrumah">Kwame Nkrumah</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a></div></div></li></ol>
